  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Puntland and Galmudug Peace Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Background: SSF has been in CARE&apos;s pipeline since 2021, gathering information on  downstream opportunities related to 5 outputs- Political settlement; Reconciliation; Democratisation &amp; local governance; Social contract; and Social contract (particularly relevant to CARE is the Social Contract element). SSF III contract for fund manager awarded in Nov/Dec 2022 to Adam Smith International.

The SSF III, launched in March 2023, aims to support inclusive political agreements, address grievances, promote democratic processes, strengthen local governance, and enhance accountability between citizens and the state. Working collaboratively with Somali authorities, civil society, and international partners is crucial for the success of the project. SSF III seeks to address the following areas of work:

1. Assembling and/or strengthening civic structures for dialogue, conciliation, and conflict resolution, aiming to empower local communities and authorities in managing conflicts and fostering trust. The project seeks to address the following areas of work:
2. Establishing Community Conciliation Forums to promote social healing and trust-building among communities, integrated with peace dividend work (addressing tangible community needs). 
3. Coordinating with other SSF III investments and partners to integrate conflict management with climate adaptation, incorporating early warning systems and community involvement. 
4. Strengthening peace journalism and media literacy to promote constructive, shared narratives, counter hate-speech and provide reliable information that fosters accountability and social trust.</narrative>
  </description>
